---
import ResponsibleAILoop from "./diagrams/ResponsibleAILoop.astro";
---
<section id="responsible-ai" class="py-20 md:py-28 border-b border-border">
  <div class="max-w-[1200px] mx-auto px-6">
    <div class="animate-on-scroll grid lg:grid-cols-[1fr_minmax(0,560px)] gap-12 lg:gap-16 items-center">
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-6">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-5 -ml-1">
          <span class="index-numeral" aria-hidden="true">03</span>
          <div class="section-label">Responsible AI</div>
        </div>

        <h2 class="font-display text-3xl md:text-[2.5rem] font-medium leading-[1.1] max-w-[30rem]">
          AI systems people can trust - <em class="text-primary italic">safe by design,</em> not by accident.
        </h2>

        <p class="text-base text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed max-w-[33rem]">
          "Responsible AI" is usually a slide from a compliance team that never shipped a model.
          For me it's an engineering loop that runs on every release.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="lg:pl-4">
        <ResponsibleAILoop />
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
